WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.827
You find a used console at a good price.

2
00:00:02.827 --> 00:00:07.337
Then the seller writes: pay me Friends and Family, no fees, and hurry.

3
00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:09.399
Pay, and you have no protection.

4
00:00:09.399 --> 00:00:11.718
Walk away, and you lose a fair deal.

5
00:00:12.317 --> 00:00:19.017
This is Handshake: a safe way to buy and sell with strangers online, on any marketplace or group chat.

6
00:00:19.617 --> 00:00:21.232
It works in three steps.

7
00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:24.799
First, AI checks the deal for scams and a fair price.

8
00:00:24.799 --> 00:00:30.048
Second, the buyer pays into a PayPal hold, so the money is reserved, not sent.

9
00:00:30.048 --> 00:00:34.490
Third, the seller is paid only when the item arrives as described.

10
00:00:35.083 --> 00:00:36.170
Here it is, live.

11
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.129
Paste the chat.

12
00:00:37.129 --> 00:00:45.375
Claude reads it and flags every trick, quoting the exact words: Friends and Family, fake urgency, and a fake PayPal invoice link.

13
00:00:45.983 --> 00:00:48.897
Channel3 checks the price against real stores.

14
00:00:48.897 --> 00:00:52.571
A sealed console at a fraction of the store price is bait.

15
00:00:52.571 --> 00:00:57.701
And Elastic remembers every scam Handshake has caught, so this one is recognised.

16
00:00:58.317 --> 00:00:59.644
Now an honest deal.

17
00:00:59.644 --> 00:01:03.834
Sam pastes his listing: no red flags, and a fair used price.

18
00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:09.212
He creates a protected deal, and sets a secret lowest price for his AI agent.

19
00:01:09.817 --> 00:01:11.794
The buyer opens Sam's link.

20
00:01:11.794 --> 00:01:16.846
They can pay through PayPal's own checkout, but the money isn't sent.

21
00:01:16.846 --> 00:01:20.653
PayPal's Orders API places an authorisation: a hold.

22
00:01:20.653 --> 00:01:22.264
Sam can see it's real.

23
00:01:22.264 --> 00:01:23.948
Nobody can take it yet.

24
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:28.947
Or the buyer backs an offer at a secret maximum, held by PayPal.

25
00:01:28.947 --> 00:01:35.542
Two AI agents negotiate from real prices, and code makes sure neither crosses its owner's limit.

26
00:01:35.542 --> 00:01:39.459
They agree, and PayPal will only ever capture that price.

27
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:40.709
Sam ships.

28
00:01:40.709 --> 00:01:46.640
The AI reads his shipping label and checks it against the buyer's PayPal-verified address.

29
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:49.013
A label to anywhere else is stopped.

30
00:01:49.013 --> 00:01:53.363
The right one passes, and EasyPost follows the parcel to the door.

31
00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.080
The buyer confirms it arrived.

32
00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:03.251
PayPal captures the payment, attaches the tracking, and pays Sam into his PayPal, after PayPal's fee.

33
00:02:03.251 --> 00:02:04.387
Damaged instead?

34
00:02:04.387 --> 00:02:09.996
A photo is priced against real parts, and PayPal captures only the fair amount.

35
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:14.145
Every deadline enforces itself with a Render Workflow.

36
00:02:14.145 --> 00:02:18.631
If Sam never ships, the hold is released and the buyer pays nothing.

37
00:02:18.631 --> 00:02:26.282
The AI advises, and code moves the money, checked by three hundred and fifteen tests and live on the PayPal sandbox.

38
00:02:26.883 --> 00:02:27.570
Handshake.

39
00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:29.837
Trust the deal, not the stranger.
